  "notes": "Governmental activities modified cash basis; business-type accrual (net position), as FY2023. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p5); operating transfers in/out 13,325 each (Total column p5). Fund balance 1,226,497 -> 1,085,573; beginning cash not printed. ending_cash = Equity in pooled cash 395,875 + Cash in bank 104,671 + County Treasurer 4,521 (p4); certificates of deposit 729,150 in ending_investments. Business-type lines from the business-type funds statement Total column (p7, titled 'Statement of Net Position - Business-Type Funds' but holding revenues/expenses); total expenses 627,952 printed on the Statement of Activities (p2); business-type 'Miscellaneous' 74,162 is a general revenue on the Statement of Activities (p3), so not charges for services. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1), Governmental and Business-Type columns, because it prints an interfund line (Due from other funds) that the governmental funds statement shows as a liability (totals differ: 1,085,573 vs 1,234,217). Detail: General, Street and Keno budget schedules (pp10-12; zero-actual budget lines included, zero-actual other financing lines omitted) plus Water, Sewer and Sanitation, Electric fund columns of p7 (no utility budget schedule). Keno operating expenses take the function the governmental funds statement prints (General government). Read pages 1-12 of 12"
